  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TA to Develop Public Procurement Infrastructure in Moldova IDF Grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Description: The Grant would be used to cover the following activities that directly relate to the shortcomings found during the CPAR: 1.   Capacity building of the National Agency for Government Procurement, including development of a comprehensive training program and training of practitioners to produce a professional procurement cadre; 2.   Improvement in the procurement process by way of preparing standardized documentation and procedures for all forms of government procurement; 3.   Measures to begin the introduction of eProcurement including: the development of a procurement website; and a performance measurement sub component to allow measurement of savings and targets and provide a national database. The project objective is to strengthen institutionl capacity for public procureement as a necessary prerequisite for successful implementation of an ambitious program of government procurement reform measures</narrative>
  </description>
